---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Season 1" description="The first Tendril season: one shared farm, one week, three medals. Dates, rules and how scores are checked.">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <p class="kicker">Tue 1 Dec to Mon 7 Dec 2026</p>
    <h1>Season 1</h1>
    <p class="lede">Everyone gets the same farm for a week. You write the program, the server replays your moves, and the
      board shows who did best. Three medals, so there is more than one way to win.</p>
    <p class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href="/play/?mode=challenge&id=week">Play the season farm</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/leaderboard/#week">See the board</a></p>

    <h2>Dates</h2>
    <p>All times are UTC.</p>
    <ul class="dates">
      <li><strong>Mon 23 Nov to Mon 30 Nov: quiet week.</strong> The game and the boards are open to early players before
        any announcement, so nobody opens an empty leaderboard on launch day.</li>
      <li><strong>Tue 1 Dec: launch.</strong> Daily challenge #1 opens, and the season is under way.</li>
      <li><strong>Mon 7 Dec, 00:00: the season closes.</strong> The season farm is a Monday-to-Monday week, so its board
        opens on Mon 30 Nov at 00:00 and runs to this point. Winners go to the Hall of Fame, and every replay opens up.</li>
      <li><strong>Tue 8 Dec: the market opens.</strong> From this day the daily farms sell at prices that move with what
        players sold the day before. The season farm is not affected. <a href="/docs/market/">How the market works</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Rules</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>One farm for everyone.</strong> The season farm has one seed, so soil, weather and orders are identical for
        every player. You start from one plot and one bot and get 6,000 ticks. A daily is 3,000.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign in with GitHub</strong> to submit. That is the only account, and the board shows your GitHub login.</li>
      <li><strong>Three medals.</strong>
        <em>Wealth</em> is the highest net worth at the end.
        <em>Speed</em> is the earliest tick at which your net worth reached par.
        <em>Brevity</em> is the fewest tokens in a program that reaches par, and needs your program attached.</li>
      <li><strong>The server decides the score.</strong> You send your moves, it plays them again on the season farm, and the
        result is what counts. An illegal move rejects the whole run. <a href="/blog/a-leaderboard-you-cant-fake/">How that works</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Resubmit as often as you like,</strong> up to the daily submission cap. Your best run for each medal is kept.
        Sending the exact same moves again is refused.</li>
      <li><strong>Replays are sealed</strong> until the season closes, so nobody can copy the leader mid-week. Your own is
        always yours to watch.</li>
      <li><strong>Programs are private</strong> unless you choose to publish one, and published programs only appear after the
        season closes.</li>
      <li><strong>Humans and models.</strong> You can write your program yourself or have an assistant write it. When you
        submit, you label the entry human or model, and boards can be filtered by that label. The label is your own word. The
        server proves a run was legal and that your program produced it. It cannot tell who wrote the program.</li>
      <li><strong>Ties.</strong> Identical runs share a rank, and the earlier submission is listed first. Otherwise ties on a
        medal go to the earlier entry.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <p>Play in the browser at <a href="/play/">the web game</a>, download the <a href="/download/">desktop app</a>, or use the
      <a href="/docs/cli/">command line</a>. New to Sprout? Start with <a href="/docs/">the docs</a>. After a run you can copy a
      share link, export a replay clip, or challenge a friend to a duel on the same farm.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

